    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>An imperial duchy created in 1395 for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#gian-galeazzo-visconti">Gian Galeazzo Visconti</a>, who briefly controlled much of northern and central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#italy">Italy</a>.</li><li>Under the Sforza it was one of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#renaissance">Renaissance</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#europe">Europe</a>’s richest courts, where Leonardo da Vinci painted the Last Supper.</li><li>Fought over in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#italian-wars">Italian Wars</a>, it was ruled by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#spain">Spain</a> from 1535 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#austria">Austria</a> from 1706 until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#napoleon">Napoleon</a> ended it in 1796–1797.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#gian-galeazzo-visconti">Gian Galeazzo Visconti</a> did not inherit his ducal title: he bought it in 1395 from Wenceslas, King of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#roman-empire">Romans</a>, for a sum reported as 100,000 florins.</p></aside>
    </section>

